My renter (elderly woman) likes to keep me aprised of her financial situation. I don't know why, but it's fine, I don't reply, I just read her emails. Today she informed me that a few months ago she ordered new checks from The Bradford Exchange (@BradfordEx). Unbeknownst to her, when she ordered those checks they enrolled her into some "club" and started charging her card $16.95 per month. She caught it a few months later, called Bradford and they immediately offered "a refund" without being specific. A month later she gets a credit for the most recent month and a confirmation of cancellation from the "club" but no refund for the previous months.

Guess where Bradford is HQ'd?  @GovPritzker's lovely state of Illinois.

@HarmeetKDhillon this type of practice should be illegal, especially when it prays upon our elderly retirees on fixed incomes.

